[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pdf-association/pdf-issues/issues/comments/1043937053","html_url":"https://github.com/pdf-association/pdf-issues/issues/157#issuecomment-1043937053","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pdf-association/pdf-issues/issues/157","id":1043937053,"node_id":"IC_kwDOEzPM4s4-OTcd","user":{"login":"datalogics-pgallot","id":1444735,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0NDQ3MzU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1444735?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/datalogics-pgallot","html_url":"https://github.com/datalogics-pgallot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/datalogics-pgallot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/datalogics-pgallot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/datalogics-pgallot/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/datalogics-pgallot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/datalogics-pgallot/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/datalogics-pgallot/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/datalogics-pgallot/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/datalogics-pgallot/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/datalogics-pgallot/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2022-02-18T05:41:32Z","updated_at":"2022-02-18T05:41:32Z","body":"I don't think nulls in color value arrays make sense, though maybe in a colorspace array...\r\n\r\nnulls are used in Destination arrays (See Table 149, section 12.3.2.2)   But those arrays have implicit sizes.  ","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pdf-association/pdf-issues/issues/comments/1043937053/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pdf-association/pdf-issues/issues/comments/1044167909","html_url":"https://github.com/pdf-association/pdf-issues/issues/157#issuecomment-1044167909","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pdf-association/pdf-issues/issues/157","id":1044167909,"node_id":"IC_kwDOEzPM4s4-PLzl","user":{"login":"MatthiasValvekens","id":6440095,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0NDAwOTU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6440095?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MatthiasValvekens","html_url":"https://github.com/MatthiasValvekens","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MatthiasValvekens/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MatthiasValvekens/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MatthiasValvekens/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MatthiasValvekens/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MatthiasValvekens/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MatthiasValvekens/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MatthiasValvekens/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MatthiasValvekens/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MatthiasValvekens/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2022-02-18T08:56:08Z","updated_at":"2022-02-18T08:56:08Z","body":"There are cases where `null`s in arrays are valid and even expected. I forget the exact rationale, but when deleting objects from the structure tree, you'll typically see `null`s being put in the **ParentTree** to avoid having to renumber everything.\r\n\r\nFor a completely different example where the spec has a \"you shall use `null`\" statement: see the description of **DecodeParms** in Table 5.\r\n\r\n>DecodeParms shall be an array with one entry for each filter in the same order as the Filter array: either the parameter \r\n> dictionary for that filter, or the null object if that filter has no parameters (or if all of its parameters have their default values). If > none of the filters have parameters, or if all their parameters have default values, the DecodeParms entry may be omitted.\r\n\r\nSo: `null`s in arrays should definitely count as indexable elements AFAICT, and I would guess that implicit nulls through nonexistent object references are no different in that regard.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pdf-association/pdf-issues/issues/comments/1044167909/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pdf-association/pdf-issues/issues/comments/1046426387","html_url":"https://github.com/pdf-association/pdf-issues/issues/157#issuecomment-1046426387","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pdf-association/pdf-issues/issues/157","id":1046426387,"node_id":"IC_kwDOEzPM4s4-XzMT","user":{"login":"petervwyatt","id":26521615,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI2NTIxNjE1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/26521615?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/petervwyatt","html_url":"https://github.com/petervwyatt","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/petervwyatt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/petervwyatt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/petervwyatt/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/petervwyatt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/petervwyatt/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/petervwyatt/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/petervwyatt/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/petervwyatt/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/petervwyatt/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2022-02-21T03:07:04Z","updated_at":"2022-02-21T03:07:04Z","body":"So I agree that for certain specific array objects in PDF there is existing wording specific to handling of `null` array entries at specific array indices. My question really pertains to all the other PDF arrays that are silent on the matter of `null` as implementation behaviours seem to differ...\r\n\r\nI also very much agree with @MatthiasValvekens (I was trying to not bias the discussion with my own opinions):\r\n> `nulls` in arrays should definitely count as indexable elements AFAICT, and I would guess that implicit nulls through nonexistent object references are no different in that regard.\r\n\r\nSo can we make a factual statement along the lines of the following (needs wordsmithing):\r\n\r\n> Whenever an implicit or explicit null object occurs as the value of an array entry (7.3.6, \"Array objects\"), the null object remains as an indexable element and does not alter the position of other array elements or the length of the array. Some PDF array objects also define specific requirements for null array elements.\"","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pdf-association/pdf-issues/issues/comments/1046426387/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pdf-association/pdf-issues/issues/comments/1046459115","html_url":"https://github.com/pdf-association/pdf-issues/issues/157#issuecomment-1046459115","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pdf-association/pdf-issues/issues/157","id":1046459115,"node_id":"IC_kwDOEzPM4s4-X7Lr","user":{"login":"datalogics-pgallot","id":1444735,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0NDQ3MzU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1444735?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/datalogics-pgallot","html_url":"https://github.com/datalogics-pgallot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/datalogics-pgallot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/datalogics-pgallot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/datalogics-pgallot/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/datalogics-pgallot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/datalogics-pgallot/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/datalogics-pgallot/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/datalogics-pgallot/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/datalogics-pgallot/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/datalogics-pgallot/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2022-02-21T04:18:18Z","updated_at":"2022-02-21T04:18:18Z","body":"I think \"implicit or explicit\" wording contradicts the null object description in 7.3.9: \"There shall be only one object of type null, denoted by the keyword null.\", unless you want to change the 7.3.9 sentence that follows to \"An indirect object reference (see 7.3.10, \"Indirect objects\") to a nonexistent object shall be treated as an _implicit_ null object.\"","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pdf-association/pdf-issues/issues/comments/1046459115/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pdf-association/pdf-issues/issues/comments/1046489399","html_url":"https://github.com/pdf-association/pdf-issues/issues/157#issuecomment-1046489399","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pdf-association/pdf-issues/issues/157","id":1046489399,"node_id":"IC_kwDOEzPM4s4-YCk3","user":{"login":"petervwyatt","id":26521615,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI2NTIxNjE1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/26521615?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/petervwyatt","html_url":"https://github.com/petervwyatt","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/petervwyatt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/petervwyatt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/petervwyatt/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/petervwyatt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/petervwyatt/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/petervwyatt/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/petervwyatt/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/petervwyatt/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/petervwyatt/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2022-02-21T05:29:07Z","updated_at":"2022-02-21T05:29:07Z","body":"Sorry - I wasn't clear. Not in 7.3.9 as that is only for dictionary objects, but added to 7.3.6 Array objects.\r\n","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pdf-association/pdf-issues/issues/comments/1046489399/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pdf-association/pdf-issues/issues/comments/1046982945","html_url":"https://github.com/pdf-association/pdf-issues/issues/157#issuecomment-1046982945","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pdf-association/pdf-issues/issues/157","id":1046982945,"node_id":"IC_kwDOEzPM4s4-Z7Eh","user":{"login":"datalogics-pgallot","id":1444735,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0NDQ3MzU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1444735?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/datalogics-pgallot","html_url":"https://github.com/datalogics-pgallot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/datalogics-pgallot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/datalogics-pgallot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/datalogics-pgallot/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/datalogics-pgallot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/datalogics-pgallot/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/datalogics-pgallot/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/datalogics-pgallot/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/datalogics-pgallot/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/datalogics-pgallot/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2022-02-21T15:15:58Z","updated_at":"2022-02-21T15:15:58Z","body":"The thing is, the \"implicit or explicit null object\" is obviously correct phrasing, because you actually can have implicit null objects (see below), but the explicit null object is defined in section 7.3.9 as a singleton (\"There shall be only one object of type null,...\"). \r\n\r\nWhich makes it weird that the next sentence implicitly  (not explicitly) defines one type of implicit null: a reference to a non-existent indirect object.  \r\n\r\nBut that's not the only type of implicit null.  There are also: \r\n- In some cases,  a value of \"0\" which is not otherwise meaningful (e.g. as a zoom factor, see the /XYZ entry in Table 149) is to be treated as a null value.   \r\n- An implicit null could also be specified in a ViewDestination dictionary by omitting the trailing array entries for a /FitV or /FitH ViewDestination.\r\n\r\nAnd I may be missing other cases.\r\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pdf-association/pdf-issues/issues/comments/1046982945/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pdf-association/pdf-issues/issues/comments/1047286482","html_url":"https://github.com/pdf-association/pdf-issues/issues/157#issuecomment-1047286482","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pdf-association/pdf-issues/issues/157","id":1047286482,"node_id":"IC_kwDOEzPM4s4-bFLS","user":{"login":"petervwyatt","id":26521615,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI2NTIxNjE1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/26521615?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/petervwyatt","html_url":"https://github.com/petervwyatt","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/petervwyatt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/petervwyatt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/petervwyatt/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/petervwyatt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/petervwyatt/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/petervwyatt/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/petervwyatt/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/petervwyatt/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/petervwyatt/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2022-02-21T23:08:06Z","updated_at":"2022-02-21T23:08:06Z","body":"I would disagree:\r\n- optional array elements are not implicit null objects. Where is that stated? They simply don't exist (don't confuse \"file format\" with how you might code something in certain programming languages). And I'm sure there are cases in PDF where we specify a default value if array elements at the end of an array don't exist.\r\n- Table 149 /XYZ is a good example where PDF defines a situation where an **explicit** `null` at certain defined indices in the array is handled in very specific ways. This is entirely covered by my proposed wording.\r\n\r\nAn implicit null arises from clause 7.3.9: \"_An indirect object reference (see 7.3.10, \"Indirect objects\") to a nonexistent object shall be treated the same as a null object_\" - i.e. where a lexically valid construct (an indirect reference) gets **treated** as a null. \r\n\r\nSo in Table 147 /XYZ if one of the _left, top, zoom_ array elements was an indirect reference to a non-existent object then the spec is very clear what a processor should do - it wouldn't be classed as an error. However, if _page_ (0-th index) was an indirect reference to a non-existent object then that would be an error, as Table 147 doesn't describe what to do.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pdf-association/pdf-issues/issues/comments/1047286482/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pdf-association/pdf-issues/issues/comments/1132206118","html_url":"https://github.com/pdf-association/pdf-issues/issues/157#issuecomment-1132206118","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pdf-association/pdf-issues/issues/157","id":1132206118,"node_id":"IC_kwDOEzPM4s5DfBgm","user":{"login":"MPBailey","id":23552720,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzNTUyNzIw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23552720?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MPBailey","html_url":"https://github.com/MPBailey","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MPBailey/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MPBailey/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MPBailey/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MPBailey/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MPBailey/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MPBailey/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MPBailey/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MPBailey/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MPBailey/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2022-05-19T21:03:21Z","updated_at":"2022-05-19T21:03:21Z","body":"I would argue that a reference from a Pages Kids object to a non-existing Page(s) object is an error. As discussed above the reference collapses to an implicit null. So now one of the items in the array is a null, and Table 30 requires all items to be indirect references to child objects. But it’s not, it’s a null. \r\n\r\nImplicit or explicit nulls in arrays are not, in themselves errors; they become errors if the specification of that array does not allow null entries.\r\n\r\nIn purely practical terms this is the best general rule anyway. Otherwise we'd have to go through and invent a lot of specific rules for what a null (implicit or explicit) means in such cases. What does a null in a Kids array in a Pages tree mean? It's not as simple as \"treat it as a blank page\" because you don't even know if it was expected to be a Pages or Page object.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pdf-association/pdf-issues/issues/comments/1132206118/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]